082 verify-shared-kv-swa: sliding-window layers on the grouped target-verify kernel

The grouped (shared-KV) verify kernel refused any layer with a sliding window, so a
hybrid model's SWA layers ran the generic extend kernel in every speculative
verify: 35 of Flint's 49 layers, ~130 us each, a depth-independent 4.6 ms of the
cycle. The prefix stage now applies the window mask itself (the rail holds the
request's last min(seq_len, window) keys; draft row l keeps key n iff
rail_len + l <= n + window, the extend kernel's rule), so causal SWA layers take
the grouped route too. SGLANG_VERIFY_SHARED_KV_SWA=0 restores the fallback.
Flint DFlash2 spec cycle 15.0 -> 11.6 ms at 34K, 21.2 -> 18.1 ms at 241K.
